\section{Conclusion}
The PASSEE and RPEC-1 architectural designs present a stable model for continuous physical-layer cryptographic data processing. By uniting non-linear wave mechanics with lock-free memory mapping and established CMOS semiconductor manufacturing standards, the engine guarantees complete phase-space isolation and predictable self-recovery performance under extreme traffic parameters.

